      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a comprehensive troubleshooting guide for resolving VPN connection timeouts at OmniCorp, designed to provide genuine solutions without unnecessary filler.\n\nFirst travelers should attempt to restart their network adapter or power cycle their router to clear any lingering traffic that is blocking the tunnel. Next, verify that your authentication credentials are up to date by resetting your username and password through the internal=admin portal to prevent identity validation errors from causing a drop-out. Users should also ensure that their firewall software on their client devices is configured to allow specific UTP traffic ports rather than blocking all incoming connections globally. If issues persist despite these checks, please contact helpdesk with a screenshot of the PSAPI output and your specific user ID so we can trace the routing logs on our server side. Finally, check if your devices are running the latest security patch set, as outdated firmware often fails to negotiate handshake protocols correctly with our secure gateway infrastructure. This thorough checklist ensures that common hardware glitches, credential rot, and protocol mismatches are systematically addressed before escalating to deeper engineering analysis. Remember to log every step taken in timesyour ticketing system to maintain a complete audit trail for future analysis if the root cause remains elusive. Proper documentation here will prevent others from encountering the same stubborn timeout scenarios while investigating complex network layer",
